# Optional CLAUDE.md snippet

For maximum reliability, append this to your `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`. The skill auto-loads via Claude Code's skills system and the addon's SessionStart hook also injects a reminder, but having it in CLAUDE.md as well gives Claude a third (system-prompt-level) signal so it can't miss the trigger.

```markdown
## Skills to invoke proactively

- **`tab-name`** — Tab naming is automatic and is NOT your job. A hook reads my prompt, asks a cheap model for a 2–3 word topic label in the language I wrote in, and applies it. Do **not** proactively rename the tab, and do not add a "renamed tab to…" line to your responses. Only act when I explicitly ask for a rename, or when a hook message tells you the automatic naming failed — then invoke the skill and follow `~/.claude/skills/tab-name/SKILL.md`.
```

`install.sh` offers to do this automatically.
